      "timeSignature": "4/4",
      "chords": [
        "I:",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "I2:",
        "D# D# Bb Bb",
        "I3:",
        "Bb Bb Bb Bb x2",
        "V1:",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "Ab Ab Ab Ab.",
        "D# D#",
        "V2:",
        "Bb Bb Bb Bb",
        "Fm Fm FmEb Ab",
        "D# D#",
        "C1:",
        "Abmaj7 Abmaj7 Abmaj7 Abmaj7",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "Abmaj7 Abmaj7 Abmaj7 Abmaj7",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "C2:",
        "Bb Bb Bb Bb",
        "Cm Cm Ab Ab",
        "Br:",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "D# D# D#",
        "Cm Cm Cm CmAb",
        "Bb Bb Fm Bb Bb",
        "Fm Ab Ab",
        "O:",
        "D# D# D# D#",
        "D# D# D#X"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "5:15 am, snow laying all around         ",
        "A collier cycles home from his night shift underground  ",
        "V2:",
        "Past the silent pub, primary school, workingman’s club                                                     ",
        "On the road from the pit-head, the churchyard packed with mining ",
        "Dead",
        "V1:",
        "Then beneath the bridge, he comes to a giant car",
        "A shroud of snow upon the roof, a Mark Ten Jaguar",
        "V2:",
        "He thought the man was fast asleep, silent, still and deep",
        "...Both dead and cold, shot through with bullet ",
        "Holes",
        "C1:",
        "The one-armed bandit man came north to fill his boots",
        "Came up from cockney-land, E-type Jags and flashy suits",
        "Put your money in, pull the levers, watch ‘em spin",
        "Cash cows in all the pubs, but he preferred the new nightclubs",
        "C2:",
        "Nineteen sixty-seven, bandit men in birdcage heaven",
        "La dolce vita, sixty-nine, all new to people of the Tyne, oh, oh",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "Who knows who did what, somebody made a call",
        "They said his hands were in the pot, that he’s been skimming hauls",
        "V2:",
        "He picks up the swag, they gaily gave away",
        "Drives his giant Jag off to his big pay day",
        "C1:",
        "...Oh the bandit man came north to fill his boots",
        "Came up from cockney-land, E-type Jags and flashy suits",
        "Yeah, the bandit man came up the great north road",
        "Up to Geordie-land, to mine the mother-lode",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "Seams blew up or cracked, black diamonds came hard won  ",
        "Generations toiled and hacked for a pittance and black lung       ",
        "V2:",
        "Crushed by tub or stone, together and alone                                                    ",
        "How the young and old, paid the price of coal",
        "C2:",
        "Eighteen sixty-seven, my angels gone to heaven",
        "He’ll be happy there, sunlight and sweet clean air, oh, oh",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "BR:",
        "They gather round the glass",
        "Tough hewers and crutters",
        "Child trappers and putters...the little foals and half-",
        "Marrows...who pushed and pulled the barrows",
        "The hod boys and the rolley-way men   ",
        "O:",
        "5:15 am"
      ]
    }
  },
