      "lyrics": [
        "I1:",
        "(Instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Caleb Meyer, he lived alone",
        "In them hollerin’ pines",
        "He made a little whiskey for himself",
        "Said it helped to pass the time",
        "V1:",
        "On one evening in back of my house",
        "Caleb come around",
        "And he called my name ‘til I came out",
        "With no one else around",
        "C:",
        "Caleb Meyer, your ghost is gonna",
        "Wear them rattlin’ chains",
        "But when I go to sleep at night",
        "Don’t you call my name",
        "I2:",
        "(Instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "Where’s your husband, Nellie Kane",
        "Where’s your darling gone?",
        "Did he go on down the mountain side",
        "And leave you all alone? Yes my",
        "V1:",
        "Husband’s gone to Bowlin’ Green to",
        "Do some business there, then",
        "Caleb threw that bottle down and",
        "Grabbed me by my hair",
        "C:",
        "Caleb Meyer, your ghost is gonna",
        "Wear them rattlin’ chains",
        "But when I go to sleep at night",
        "Don’t you call my name",
        "I3:",
        "(Instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "He threw me in the needle bed",
        "Across my dress he lay, then he",
        "Pinned my hands above my head and",
        "I commenced to pray, I cried",
        "V1:",
        "“My God, I am your child",
        "Send your angels down” then",
        "Feelin’ with my fingertips the",
        "Bottle neck I found, I",
        "V1:",
        "Drew that glass across his neck as",
        "Fine as any blade and I",
        "Felt his blood pour fast and hot",
        "Around me where I lay",
        "I3:",
        "(Instrumental)",
        "I3:",
        "(Instrumental)",
        "C:",
        "Caleb Meyer, your ghost is gonna",
        "Wear them rattlin’ chains",
        "But when I go to sleep at night",
        "Don’t you call my name",
        "O:",
        "Caleb Meyer, your ghost is gonna",
        "Wear them rattlin’ chains",
        "But when I go to sleep at night",
        "Don’t you call my name"
      ]
    }
