        "V:",
        "(Oh the) smell of the bakery from across the street, got in my nose, yeah",
        "As we carried our ladders down the street with the wrought iron gate rows",
        "I went home and listened to Jimmie Rodgers in my lunch break",
        "Bought five woodbines at the shop on the corner and went straight back to work",
        "V2:",
        "Sam was up on top and I was on the bottom with the V",
        "We went for lemonade and Paris burns at the shop and broke for tea, watch out",
        "I collected from the lady and I cleaned the fan light inside out",
        "I was blowing saxophone on the weekend in that down joint",
        "C:",
        "(What's my) line? I'm happy cleaning windows...take my ",
        "Time, I'll see you when my love grows...baby, don't let it ",
        "Slide, I'm a working man in my prime, cleaning windows, number 36",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental solo) ",
        "V2:",
        "I heard Leadbelly and Blind Lemon on the street where I was born, yeah",
        "Sonny Terry, Brownie Mcghee and Muddy Waters singing \"I'm a rollin' stone\"",
        "I went home and read my Christmas Humphrey's book on Zen",
        "\"Curiosity Killed the Cat\", Kerouac's \"Dharma Bums\" and \"On the Road\"",
