  {
    "file": "Diamond Joe.songlyrics",
    "lastModifiedDate": 1763368213563,
    "song": {
      "title": "Diamond Joe",
      "artist": "Cisco Houston",
      "coverArtist": "Charlie Crockett",
      "user": "Jonathan B.",
      "dateCreated": 1740544433024,
      "lastModifiedDate": 1763368213563,
      "copyright": "1952 Traditional folk, written by Baldwin Hawes, originally performed on stage by Cisco Houston",
      "key": "Bb",
      "defaultBpm": 105,
      "timeSignature": "2/4",
      "chords": [
        "I1:",
        "Bb Bb Bb Bb",
        "I2:",
        "Bb Bb Bb Bb",
        "Bb Bb Gm Gm",
        "Bb Bb Bb Gm",
        "Bb Gm Bb Bb",
        "Bb Bb",
        "V:",
        "Bb Gm Gm Eb Bb Bb x4",
        "O:",
        "Bb Bb BbX"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I1:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "There is a man you'll hear about, most any place you go",
        "And his holdings are in Texas, and his name is Diamond Joe",
        "He carries all his money, in a diamond-studded jar",
        "An' he never was much bothered, by the process of the law",
        "I1:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "I hired out to Diamond Joe boys, I did offer him my hand",
        "And he gave me a string of horses, so old they couldn't stand",
        "I'd likely to starve to death boys, he did mistreat me so",
        "I never saved a dollar, in the pay of Diamond Joe",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now, his bread it was corn dodger, and his meat I couldn't chaw",
        "And he kept me well distracted, with the wagging of his jaw",
        "And the telling of his story, I aim to let you know",
        "There never was a rounder, who lied like Diamond Joe",
        "I1:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now, I tried three times to quit him boys, but he did argue so",
        "And I'm still punching cattle, in the pay of Diamond Joe",
        "But when I'm called up a'yonder, and come my time to go",
        "Give my blankets to my buddies, and give the fleas to Diamond Joe",
        "O:",
        "(instrumental)"
      ]
    }
  },
