      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V1:",
        "(I've seen the) bright lights of Memphis and the Commodore Hotel, and",
        "Underneath a street lamp, I met a southern belle, oh she ",
        "Took me to the river, where she cast her spell, and ",
        "In that southern moonlight, she sang this song so well",
        "C:",
        "(If you'll) be my Dixie chicken I'll be your Tennessee lamb, and",
        "We can walk together down in Dixieland, down in ",
        "Dixieland",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V2:",
        "We made all the hotspots, my money flowed like wine, then the",
        "Low-down southern whiskey, yeah, began to fog my mind, and I",
        "Don't remember church bells, or the money I put down, on the ",
        "White picket fence and boardwalk, on the house at the end of town, oh but",
        "Boy do I remember the strain of her refrain, and the ",
        "Nights we spent together, and the way she called my name",
        "C:",
        "(If you'll) be my Dixie chicken I'll be your Tennessee lamb, and",
        "We can walk together down in Dixieland, down in ",
        "Dixieland",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V2:",
        "(Well it's) many years since she ran away, yes that guitar player sure could play",
        "She always liked to sing along, she always handy with a song",
        "Then one night at the lobby of the Commodore Hotel, I ",
        "Chanced to meet a bartender who said he knew her well, and",
        "As he handed me a drink he began to hum a song, and",
        "All the boys there, at the bar, began to sing along",
        "C:",
        "(If you'll) be my Dixie chicken I'll be your Tennessee lamb, and",
        "We can walk together down in Dixieland, down in ",
        "Dixieland",
        "O:",
        ""
      ]
    }
