        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now, many many years ago when I was twenty three, I was",
        "Married to a widow who was pretty as could be, this",
        "Widow had a grown-up daughter had hair of red, my",
        "Father fell in love with her and soon the two were wed, this",
        "V:",
        "Made my dad my son-in-law and changed my very life, my",
        "Daughter was my mother 'cause she was my father's wife, to",
        "Complicate the matters even though it brought me joy, I",
        "Soon became the father of a bouncing baby boy, my",
        "V:",
        "Little baby then became a brother-in-law to dad, and",
        "So became my uncle though it made me very sad, for",
        "If he was my uncle that also made him the brother, of the",
        "Widow's grown-up daughter who, of course, was my step-mother",
