        "AE7 A"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(talking) These are the times that try men's souls",
        "In the course of our nation's history",
        "The people of Boston have rallied bravely",
        "Whenever the rights of men have been threatened",
        "Today, a new crisis has arisen",
        "The Metropolitan Transit Authority better known as the MTA is ",
        "Attempting to levy a burdensome tax on the population",
        "In the form of a subway fare increase",
        "Citizens, hear me out, this could happen to you",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental banjo)",
        "V:",
        "(Well let me) tell you of the story of a man named Charlie on a",
        "Tragic and fateful day, he put ",
        "Ten cents in his pocket, kissed his wife and family went to ",
        "Ride on the MTA",
        "C:",
        "(Well did he) ever return? No he never returned and his",
        "Fate is still unlearned (what a pity) He may ",
        "Ride forever 'neath the streets of Boston, he's the ",
        "Man who never returned",
        "V:",
        "(Charlie) handed in his dime at the Kendall Square station and he",
        "Changed for Jamaica Plain, when he ",
        "Got there the conductor told him, \"one more nickel\" Charlie ",
        "Couldn't get off of that train",
        "C:",
        "(But did he) ever return? No he never returned and",
        "His fate is still unlearned (poor old Charlie), he may Ride forever 'neath the streets of Boston, he's the ",
        "Man who never returned",
        "V:",
        "(Now) all night long Charlie rides through the station crying",
        "\"What will become of me? How ",
        "Can I afford to see my sister in Chelsea or my ",
        "Cousin in Roxbury?\"",
        "C:",
        "(But did he) ever return? No he never returned and",
        "His fate is still unlearned (shame and scandal), he may Ride forever 'neath the streets of Boston, he's the ",
        "Man who never returned",
        "V:",
        "(Charlie's) wife goes down to the Scollay Square station every",
        "Day at quarter past two, and ",
        "Through the open window she hands Charlie a sandwich as the ",
        "Train comes rumbling through!",
        "C:",
        "(But did he) ever return? No he never returned and His fate is still unlearned (he may ride forever), he may Ride forever 'neath the streets of Boston, he's the",
        "Man who never returned",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental banjo)",
        "V:",
        "(Now you) citizens of Boston, don't you think it's a scandal, how the",
        "People have to pay and pay? Fight the ",
        "Fare increase, vote for George O'Brian, get poor ",
        "Charlie off the MTA",
        "V:",
        "(Or else he'll) never return, no he'll never return and",
        "His fate is still unlearned (just like Paul Revere), he may Ride forever 'neath the streets of Boston, he's the",
        "Man who never returned",
        "T:",
        "(He's the) man who never returned, he's the",
        "Man who never returned, he's the ",
        "Man who never returned"
      ]
    }
