      "lyrics": [
        "I1:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Before 1980, me ’n' my lady drove a ",
        "Ford station wagon going South",
        "There by the blue sea, sweet days that seem long gone",
        "Fill me like wine in my mouth",
        "V:",
        "At a Shell station I stole her a phonebook of ",
        "Monterey County and Big Sur",
        "So then at her leisure, she could call about another look at the ",
        "Places that I went with her",
        "C:",
        "I don’t know when I’ll be wanderin’ again through the ",
        "Seaweed and rocks by the shore, and",
        "I don’t know if I will stand on the cliffs lookin’ ",
        "Down at the green ocean’s roar, oh, oh, oh, anymore",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Worn out warehouses and visions of Steinbeck ",
        "Kept us on Cannery Row",
        "Nearby the crabs crawled on barnacles goose-necked,  we ",
        "Watched, with the tide risin’ slow",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Later that evenin’ at an inn by the stream’s end",
        "The waiter gave his smile out for free, his",
        "Manner so easy our eyes found quite pleasin’, we ",
        "Laughed, at his thumb in the tea",
        "V:",
        "At a Shell station I stole her a phonebook of ",
        "Monterey County and Big Sur",
        "So now that she’s left me, I can call about another look at the",
        "Places that I went with her, and",
        "C:",
        "I don’t know when I’ll be wanderin’ again through the ",
        "Seaweed and rocks by the shore, and",
        "I don’t know if I will stand on the cliffs lookin’ ",
        "Down at the green ocean’s roar, oh, oh, oh, anymore",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "O:",
        "At a Shell station, I stole her a phonebook of ",
        "Monterey County and Big Sur",
        "",
        "",
        ""
      ]
