  {
    "file": "(Nothing But) Flowers.songlyrics",
    "lastModifiedDate": 1763368404257,
    "song": {
      "title": "(Nothing But) Flowers",
      "artist": "Talking Heads, The",
      "user": "Jonathan B.",
      "dateCreated": 1712551544204,
      "lastModifiedDate": 1763368404257,
      "copyright": "1988 EMI",
      "key": "C",
      "defaultBpm": 124,
      "timeSignature": "4/4",
      "chords": [
        "I1:",
        "X X X X x2",
        "I2:",
        "C GF C GF x2",
        "I3:",
        "C GF C GF",
        "I4:",
        "DDsus2/E AG DDsus2/E AG x8",
        "V:",
        "C C Em Em",
        "Dm Dm G G",
        "C C Em Em",
        "Dm Dm G G",
        "PC:",
        "B Em B Em",
        "C Em F G",
        "C1:",
        "C GF C GF x2",
        "C2:",
        "DDsus2/E AG DDsus2/E AG x2",
        "C3:",
        "DDsus2/E AG DDsus2/E AG x3",
        "DDsus2/E AG DX",
        "Br:",
        "Dm A Dm A",
        "Fm C Fm G"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I1:",
        "(instrumental latin percussion)",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Here we stand, like an Adam and Eve",
        "Waterfalls, the Garden of Eden",
        "Two fools in love, so beautiful and strong",
        "Birds in the trees, are smiling upon them",
        "PC:",
        "From the age of the dinosaurs cars have run on gasoline",
        "Where? Where have they gone? Now, it's nothing but flowers",
        "C1:",
        "There was a factory, now there are mountains and rivers (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "We caught a rattlesnake, now we've got something for dinner (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "C2:",
        "There was a shopping mall, now it's all covered with flowers (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "If this is paradise, I wish I had a lawn mower (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Years ago, I was an angry young man",
        "I'd pretend, that I was a billboard",
        "Standing tall, by the side of the road",
        "I fell in love, with the beautiful highway",
        "PC:",
        "This used to be real estate, now it's only fields and trees",
        "Where? Where is the town? Now, it's nothing but flowers",
        "BR:",
        "The highways and cars, were sacrificed for agriculture",
        "I thought that we'd start over, but I guess I was wrong",
        "C1:",
        "Once there were parking lots, now it's a peaceful oasis (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "This was a Pizza Hut, now it's all covered with daisies (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "C2:",
        "I miss the honky tonks, Dairy Queens, and 7-Elevens (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "And as things fell apart, nobody paid much attention (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "I4:",
        "(instrumental solo)",
        "C3:",
        "I dream of cherry pies, candy bars, and chocolate chip cookies (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "We used to microwave, now we just eat nuts and berries (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "This was a discount store, now it's turned into a cornfield (you've got it, you've got it)",
        "Don't leave me stranded here, I can't get used to this lifestyle"
      ]
    }
  },
