  {
    "file": "Ordinary Man.songlyrics",
    "lastModifiedDate": 1773041016000,
    "song": {
      "title": "Ordinary Man",
      "artist": "Christy Moore",
      "user": "Colin L.",
      "dateCreated": 1759159801505,
      "lastModifiedDate": 1773041016000,
      "copyright": "1985 Walker Music UK, written by Peter Hames",
      "key": "C",
      "defaultBpm": 95,
      "timeSignature": "4/4",
      "chords": [
        "I:",
        "Am G F Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "Am G F Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "I2:",
        "F G Am Am",
        "A:",
        "Am G F Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "Am G F Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "B:",
        "F G CG/B Am",
        "F F E E7",
        "Am G F Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "F G Am Am",
        "O:",
        "F G Am Am x2"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "A:",
        "I'm an ordinary man, nothing special, nothing grand",
        "I've had to work for everything I own",
        "I never asked for a lot, I was happy with what I got",
        "Enough to keep my family and my home",
        "B:",
        "They say that times are hard and they've handed me my cards",
        "They say there's not the work to go around",
        "And when the whistle blows, the gates will finally close",
        "Tonight they're going to shut this factory down, and they'll tear it",
        "Down",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "A:",
        "I never missed a day, nor went on strike for better pay",
        "For 20 years I served them best I could",
        "Now with a handshake and a check it seems so easy to forget",
        "Loyalty through the bad times and the good",
        "B:",
        "The owner says he's sad to see that things have got so bad",
        "But the captains of industry won't let him lose",
        "He still smokes his cigar and drives a brand new car",
        "And still takes his family on a cruise, he'll never",
        "Lose",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "A:",
        "Now it seems to me such a cruel irony, he's",
        "Richer now than ever he was before",
        "Now my check is spent and I can't afford the rent, there's",
        "One law for the rich, one for the poor",
        "B:",
        "Every day I've tried to salvage some of my pride, to",
        "find some work so's I might pay my way",
        "Oh but everywhere I go, the answers always no",
        "No work for anyone here today, no work",
        "Today",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental) No work today",
        "A:",
        "And so condemned I stand, just an ordinary man, like",
        "thousands beside me in the queue",
        "I watch my darling wife trying to make the best of life, God",
        "Knows what the kids are going to do",
        "B:",
        "Now that we are faced with this human waste",
        "Generations cast aside, for as",
        "Long as I live, I never will forgive, you've",
        "Stripped me of my dignity and pride, you stripped me",
        "Bare, you've stripped me bare",
        "O:",
        "No work today, no work",
        "Today"
      ]
    }
  },
