      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Living on the road my friend",
        "Was gonna keep you free and clean",
        "Now you wear your skin like iron and your",
        "Breath's as hard as kerosene",
        "Weren't your mama's only boy but her",
        "Favorite one it seems...she",
        "Began to cry when you said goodbye, and ",
        "Sank into your dreams",
        "V:",
        "Pancho was a bandit, boys, his ",
        "Horse was fast as polished steel",
        "He wore his gun outside his pants, for",
        "All the honest world to feel",
        "But Pancho met his match you know, on the",
        "Deserts down in Mexico, and",
        "Nobody heard his dying words, ah but",
        "That's the way it goes",
        "C:",
        "And all the Federales say",
        "They could have had him any day",
        "They only let him hang around",
        "Out of kindness I suppose",
        "V:",
        "Lefty, he can't sing the blues",
        "All night long like he used to",
        "The dust that Pancho bit down south",
        "Ended up in Lefty's mouth",
        "The day they laid poor Pancho low",
        "Lefty split for Ohio",
        "Where he got the bread to go",
        "Ah there ain't nobody knows",
        "C:",
        "And all the Federales say",
        "They could have had him any day",
        "They only let him slip away",
        "Out of kindness, I suppose",
        "V:",
        "Well the poets tell how Pancho fell",
        "And Lefty's living in a cheap hotel",
        "The desert's quiet and Cleveland's cold",
        "So the story ends we're told",
        "Pancho needs your prayers it's true",
        "But save a few for Lefty too",
        "He just did what he had to do",
        "And now he's growing old",
        "C:",
        "A few grey Federales say",
        "They could have had him any day",
        "They only let him go so long, out of",
        "Kindness, I suppose",
        "O:",
        "A few grey Federales say",
        "They could have had him any day",
        "They only let him go so long, out of",
