      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Buddy I went down to Scarlet Town, ain’t never been there before",
        "Well, you slept on a feather bed, I slept on the floor",
        "V:",
        "Now I don’t mind a little town, or drinking my coffee cold",
        "But the things I seen in Scarlet Town, did mortify my soul",
        "C:",
        "Well, look at that deep well, look at that that dark grave",
        "Ringing that iron bell in Scarlet Town today",
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now I spent some time in New Orleans and in Cairo on a bend",
        "But Scarlet Town brought me down, low as I ever been",
        "C:",
        "Ahh, look at that deep well, look at that that dark grave",
        "Ringing that iron bell in Scarlet Town today",
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "On the day I came to Scarlet Town, you promised I’d be your bride",
        "But you left me here to rot away like holly on a mountainside",
        "C:",
        "Ahh, look at that deep well, look at that that dark grave",
        "Ringing that iron bell in Scarlet Town today",
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now you may hide in Scarlet Town for a hundred years or more",
        "But the man who knows what time it is is knocking at the door",
        "V:",
        "So fare you well, my own true love if you ever see me around",
        "I’ll be looking through a telescope from hell to Scarlet Town",
        "C:",
        "Now, look at that deep well, look at that that dark grave",
        "Ringing that iron bell in Scarlet Town today",
        "O:",
        "(instrumental)"
      ]
    }
