  {
    "file": "She.songlyrics",
    "lastModifiedDate": 1705642551403,
    "song": {
      "title": "She",
      "artist": "Charles Aznavour",
      "coverArtist": "Elvis Costello",
      "user": "David L.",
      "dateCreated": 1705642551403,
      "lastModifiedDate": 1705642551403,
      "copyright": "1974 Mercury Records, Island Records, written by Charles Aznavour, Herbert Kretzmer 1974",
      "key": "Db",
      "defaultBpm": 66,
      "timeSignature": "4/4",
      "chords": [
        "I:",
        "DbDb/F GbAb",
        "I2:",
        "Db Edim7 Gb DbBb/D",
        "Ebm Gbm/A Db Eb/GAb",
        "Db",
        "V:",
        "Db Edim7 Gb DbBb/D",
        "Ebm Gbm/A Db Eb/GAb",
        "DbGbGb/AbAb",
        "V2:",
        "Db Edim7 Gb DbBb/D",
        "Ebm Gbm/A Db Eb/GAb",
        "B:",
        "A E D Db",
        "GbmB EDb Eb EbAb",
        "O:",
        "Gb Db/F Ebm Db"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "V:",
        "She may be the face I can't forget, a trace of pleasure or regret, may be my treasure or the price I have to pay",
        "She may be the song that summer sings, may be the chill that autumn brings, may be a hundred different things, within the measure of a day.",
        "V:",
        "She may be the beauty or the beast, may be the famine or the feast, may turn each day into a heaven or a hell",
        "She may be the mirror of my dreams, a smile reflected in a stream, she may not be what she may seem inside her shell",
        "I2:",
        "B:",
        "She who always seems so happy in a crowd, whose eyes can be so private and so proud, no one's allowed to see them when they cry",
        "She may be the love that cannot hope to last, may come to me from shadows of the past, that I'll remember till the day I die",
        "V2:",
        "She may be the reason I survive, the why and wherefore I'm alive, the one I'll care for through the rough and ready years",
        "Me I'll take her laughter and her tears, and make them all my souvenirs, for where she goes I've got to be the meaning of my life is",
        "O:",
        "She, she, she"
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "file": "Shelter from the Storm.songlyrics",
    "lastModifiedDate": 1672207715720,
    "song": {
      "title": "Shelter from the Storm",
      "artist": "Bob Dylan",
      "user": "Shari C.",
      "dateCreated": 1672207715720,
      "lastModifiedDate": 1672207715720,
      "copyright": "1975 Columbia",
      "key": "E",
      "defaultBpm": 106,
      "timeSignature": "2/4",
      "chords": [
        "I:",
        "E E E E",
        "E E/B E E/B",
        "I2:",
        "E Emaj9 A E x2",
        "I3:",
        "E Emaj9 A E E",
        "I4:",
        "E Emaj9 A E",
        "E Emaj9 A E E",
        "I5:",
        "E Emaj9/D# A",
        "I6:",
        "E Emaj9 A A x3",
        "E Emaj9 A E",
        "V:",
        "E Emaj9 A E",
        "E Emaj9 A A/E",
        "E Emaj9 A A",
        "E Emaj9 A",
        "O:",
        "E Emaj9 A A x3",
        "E Emaj9 A E"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "'Twas in another lifetime one of toil and blood",
        "When blackness was a virtue, the road was full of mud",
        "I came in from the wilderness a creature void of form",
        "\"Come in\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "And if I pass this way again you can rest assured",
        "I'll always do my best for her on that I give my word",
        "In a world of steel-eyed death and men who are fighting to be warm",
        "\"Come in\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I3:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Not a word was spoke between us there was little risk involved",
        "Everything up to that point had been left unresolved",
        "Try imagining a place where it's always safe and warm",
        "\"Come in\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I4:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "I was burned out from exhaustion buried in the hail",
        "Poisoned in the bushes and blown out on the trail",
        "Hunted like a crocodile ravaged in the corn",
        "\"Come in\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Suddenly I turned around and she was standing there",
        "With silver bracelets on her wrists and flowers in her hair",
        "She walked up to me so gracefully and took my crown of thorns",
        "\"Come in,\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Now there's a wall between us something there's been lost",
        "I took too much for granted, I got my signals crossed",
        "Just to think that it all began on an uneventful morn",
        "\"Come in,\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Well the deputy walks on hard nails and the preacher rides a mount",
        "But nothing really matters much it's doom alone that counts",
        "And the one-eyed undertaker he blows a futile horn",
        "\"Come in,\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "I've heard newborn babies wailing like a mourning dove",
        "And old men with broken teeth stranded without love",
        "Do I understand your question man, is it hopeless and forlorn?",
        "\"Come in,\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "In a little hilltop village they gambled for my clothes",
        "I bargained for salvation and she gave me a lethal dose",
        "I offered up my innocence, I got repaid with scorn",
        "\"Come in\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I2:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "Well I'm living in a foreign country but I'm bound to cross the line",
        "Beauty walks a razor's edge someday I'll make it mine",
        "If I could only turn back the clock to when God and her were born",
        "\"Come in,\" she said \"I'll give you shelter from the storm\"",
        "I5:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "I6:",
        "(instrumental harmonica)",
        "O:",
        "(instrumental)"
      ]
    }
  },
