        "CG C G G"
      ],
      "lyrics": [
        "I:",
        "(instrumental)",
        "V:",
        "As I was a going over the far famed Kerry mountains",
        "I met with Captain Farrell and his money he was counting",
        "I first produced my pistol and I then produced my rapier",
        "Saying \"Stand and deliver\" for he were a bold deceiver, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar",
        "V:",
        "I counted out his money and it made a pretty penny",
        "I put it in me pocket and I took it home to Jenny",
        "She sighed and she swore, that she never would deceive me",
        "But the devil take the women for they never can be easy, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar",
        "V:",
        "I went up to my chamber, all for to take a slumber",
        "I dreamt of gold and jewels and for sure it was no wonder",
        "But Jenny drew me charges and she filled them up with water",
        "Then sent for Captain Farrell to be ready for the slaughter, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar",
        "V:",
        "('Twas was) early in the morning, just before I rose to travel",
        "Up comes a band of footmen and likewise Captain Farrell",
        "I first produced me pistol for she stolen away me rapier",
        "But I couldn't shoot the water, so a prisoner I was taken, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar",
        "V:",
        "(Now there's) some take delight in the carriages a-rolling",
        "And others take delight in the hurling and the bowling",
        "But I take delight in the juice of the barley, and",
        "Courting pretty fair maids in the morning bright and early, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for the daddy-o",
        "Whack for the daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar",
        "V:",
        "If anyone can aid me it is my brother in the army",
        "If I can find his station in Cork or in Killarney, and",
        "If he'll go with me, we'll go roving through Killkenny, and I'm",
        "Sure he'll treat me better than my own a-sporting Jenny, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C2:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar, mush-a ",
        "Ring dum do dum da",
        "C:",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "Whack for my daddy-o",
        "There's whiskey in the jar"
      ]
    }
